-- title:
--   Transfer data at a twisted class with elliptic norm
-- statement:
--   The setting is a Galois extension $L/K$ of number fields of prime degree $[L:K]$ (hypothesis `hprime`), with a fixed $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$, $\sigma \neq 1$, such that every element of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the cyclic subgroup generated by $\sigma^{-1}$ (hypothesis `hgen`); the twisting everywhere below is by $\sigma^{-1} =$ `σ.symm`. Two real parameters $0 < \alpha < \beta$ delimit a band of determinant norms. Haar measures $\nu_{Z_L}$ on $(\mathbb{A}_L)^\times$ and $\nu_{Z_K}$ on $(\mathbb{A}_K)^\times$ are given, as is a datum $D$ (an [`M4aHerbrand.IdeleGaloisDescent`](def/M4aHerbrand_IdeleClassVocab.html#L28)), that is, a homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ to the ring automorphisms of $\mathbb{A}_L$ which is compatible with $L \to \mathbb{A}_L$ and continuous in each element.
--
--   Character data: $\xi_L$ is a homomorphism from the full subgroup of $(\mathbb{A}_L)^\times$ to $\mathbb{C}^\times$, continuous as a $\mathbb{C}$-valued function (`hξc`) and trivial on the principal ideles, i.e. on the range of $L^\times \to (\mathbb{A}_L)^\times$ (`hξt`); $\Xi$ is a finite set of homomorphisms from the full subgroup of $(\mathbb{A}_K)^\times$ to $\mathbb{C}^\times$, and `hΞ` states that a character $\xi$ belongs to $\Xi$ precisely when it is continuous, trivial on the principal ideles of $K$, and satisfies $\xi \circ N = \xi_L$, where $N$ is the idelic norm `idelicNorm` of the base-change datum `genuineBaseChange K L` (the unit group map induced by the algebra norm of $\mathbb{A}_L$ over $\mathbb{A}_K$).
--
--   Twisted class data on the $L$-side: $R_L$ is a set of elements of $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ contained in the set of those $\delta$ for which there is a $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ that is either elliptic (its characteristic polynomial has no root in $K$, `ellipticCell`) or central (a scalar matrix, `centralCell`), with `normClassMap hgen` of the $\sigma^{-1}$-twisted class of $\delta$ equal to the conjugacy class of $\gamma$; here `normClassMap` sends the twisted class of $\delta$ (for the relation $\delta' = k^{-1}\delta\,\sigma^{-1}(k)$) to the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$-conjugacy class of an element whose image in $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ is conjugate to the twisted norm of $\delta$ (hypothesis `hRLsub`). Hypothesis `hRL` states that every $\delta$ in that set has a unique $\delta_0 \in R_L$ for which $\delta = \mathrm{scalar}(u)\,(h^{-1}\delta_0\,\sigma^{-1}(h))$ for some $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ and $u \in L^\times$. For each $\delta_0 \in R_L$, $\Psi_L(\delta_0)$ is a subset of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ contained in the band $\{g : \|\det g\|_{\mathbb{A}_L} \in [\alpha,\beta]\}$, where $\|\cdot\|$ is `TateGlobal.ideleNorm` (the scaling factor of Haar measure) (`hΨLs`), and is a fundamental domain for the image under `globalPoints` of the $\sigma^{-1}$-twisted centraliser $\{t \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L) : t\,\delta_0\,\sigma^{-1}(t)^{-1} = \delta_0\}$, with respect to the adelic Haar measure `adelicGLHaar` restricted to that band (`hΨL`). Further, $\Theta \subseteq (\mathbb{A}_L)^\times$ is a fundamental domain, for $\nu_{Z_L}$, of the range of the homomorphism $u \mapsto \sigma^{-1}(u)/u$ from $L^\times$ followed by $L^\times \to (\mathbb{A}_L)^\times$ (`hΘ`).
--
--   Class data on the $K$-side: $R_K \subseteq \mathrm{centralCell}\,K \cup \mathrm{ellipticCell}\,K$ (`hRKsub`), and `hRK` states that every central or elliptic $\gamma$ has a unique $\gamma_0 \in R_K$ with $\gamma = \mathrm{scalar}(a)(h^{-1}\gamma_0 h)$ for some $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K)$, $a \in K^\times$. For $\gamma_0 \in R_K$, $\Psi_K(\gamma_0)$ lies in the band $\{g : \|\det g\|_{\mathbb{A}_K} \in [\alpha,\beta]\}$ (`hΨKs`) and is a fundamental domain for the image under `globalPoints` of the centraliser of $\gamma_0$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$, for `adelicGLHaar` restricted to that band (`hΨK`).
--
--   Comparison constants: $c_0 \in \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}$ and $\kappa > 0$, where `hκl` asserts that for every measurable $g : (\mathbb{A}_K)^\times \to \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}^\infty$ the lower integral of $g \circ N$ over $\Theta$ against $\nu_{Z_L}$ equals $\kappa$ times the integral of $g$ over the range of $N$ against $\nu_{Z_K}$, and `hκi` asserts the corresponding statement for measurable $\mathbb{C}$-valued $g$, namely the equivalence of integrability of $g \circ N$ on $\Theta$ with integrability of $g$ on the range of $N$, together with the same identity of integrals with factor $\kappa$.
--
--   Test functions and matching: $\varphi$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ and $f$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ are continuous with compact support. Hypothesis `hOn` is `AreMatchingOn` for $K$, $L$, $\mathbb{A}_K$ and $\sigma^{-1}$, with the measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K)$ obtained by pushing `adelicGLHaar` on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ forward along the $\mathrm{GL}_2$-map of the inverse of the ring isomorphism $L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K \cong \mathbb{A}_K \otimes_K L \cong \mathbb{A}_L$ (`Algebra.TensorProduct.comm` followed by [`M4aHerbrand.Bridge.genuineRingEquiv`](def/M4aHerbrand_GenuineTensorEquiv.html#L57)), with $c_0 \cdot$ `adelicGLHaar` on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$, and with test functions $\varphi$ transported along the same isomorphism, and $f$. Unfolded, `AreMatchingOn` has two clauses: first, whenever the twisted norm string $\delta\,\sigma^{-1}(\delta)\cdots$ of $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K)$ is regular semisimple, $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ is regular semisimple, $y$ conjugates the image of $\gamma$ into that norm string, and Haar measures on the centraliser of $\gamma$ and on the twisted centraliser of $\delta$ are coupled through $y$, any twisted orbital integral $I'$ of $\varphi$ and any orbital integral $I$ of $f$ agree; second, for regular semisimple $\gamma$ which is not a twisted norm, every orbital integral of $f$ at $\gamma$ vanishes.
--
--   Vanishing hypothesis `hvan`: for every $\gamma_0 \in R_K$ that is elliptic, every $a \in K^\times$ and every idele $u$ of $K$ such that the conjugacy class of $\mathrm{scalar}(a)\gamma_0$ is not in the range of `normClassMap hgen`, and such that there exists $c \in (L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K)^\times$ whose twisted norm string at the scalar matrix $c$ equals the image of the central scalar $u$ under `toTensorGL`, every Haar measure $\tau$ on the centraliser in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ of $\mathrm{globalPoints}(\gamma_0)\cdot\mathrm{scalar}(\hat{a}u)$ (with $\hat{a}$ the idele attached to $a$) and every $I \in \mathbb{C}$ that is an orbital integral of $f$ at that element for $c_0 \cdot$ `adelicGLHaar` and $\tau$ satisfies $I = 0$.
--
--   Finally, $\delta_0 \in R_L$, $\gamma_0 \in R_K$ elliptic, $a \in K^\times$, and `hNcl` states that `normClassMap hgen` of the $\sigma^{-1}$-twisted class of $\delta_0$ is the conjugacy class of $\mathrm{scalar}(a)\gamma_0$.
--
--   The conclusion asserts the existence of a measure $\tau'$ on the twisted centraliser $T' = \{t \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L) : t\,\mathrm{globalPoints}(\delta_0)\,(\sigma^{-1}_D t)^{-1} = \mathrm{globalPoints}(\delta_0)\}$, where $\sigma^{-1}_D$ is the action of $\sigma^{-1}$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ induced by $D$, of a measure $\tau$ on the centraliser $T$ of $\mathrm{globalPoints}(\gamma_0)$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$, and of $C \in \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}^\infty$, such that $\tau'$ is a Haar measure, s-finite and right invariant, $\tau$ is a Haar measure, s-finite and right invariant, $C \neq 0$ and $C \neq \infty$, and furthermore the following four statements hold.
--
--   First, for every subset $D_m$ of $T$ which is a fundamental domain, for $\tau$, of the opposite group of the subgroup of $T$ corresponding to the image under `globalPoints` of the centraliser of $\gamma_0$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$, and for all reals $0 < A \leq B$,
--   $$\tau\bigl(D_m \cap \{t : \|\det t\|_{\mathbb{A}_K} \in [A,B]\}\bigr) = C \cdot \log(B/A).$$
--
--   Second, for every subset $D_m'$ of $T'$ which is a fundamental domain, for $\tau'$, of the opposite group of the subgroup of $T'$ corresponding to the image under `globalPoints` of the $\sigma^{-1}$-twisted centraliser $\{t \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L) : t\,\delta_0\,\sigma^{-1}(t)^{-1} = \delta_0\}$, and for all reals $0 < A \leq B$,
--   $$\tau'\bigl(D_m' \cap \{t : \|\det t\|_{\mathbb{A}_L} \in [A,B]\}\bigr) = C \cdot \frac{\log(B/A)}{[L:K]}.$$
--
--   Third, for every idele $z \in (\mathbb{A}_L)^\times$ there is a function $w$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$, non-negative, measurable and compactly supported, which is a section function for the twisted integrand in the sense that for every $x$ with $\varphi\bigl(x^{-1}\,\mathrm{globalPoints}(\delta_0)\,\sigma^{-1}_D(\mathrm{scalar}(z)\,x)\bigr) \neq 0$ one has $\int_{T'} w(t\,x)\,d\tau'(t) = 1$, and which satisfies: for every $I \in \mathbb{C}$ that is an orbital integral, in the sense of `IsOrbitalIntegralOn` for $\mathbb{A}_K$, the measure $c_0 \cdot$ `adelicGLHaar`, the element $\mathrm{globalPoints}(\gamma_0)$ and the measure $\tau$, of the function $g \mapsto f\bigl(g\,\mathrm{scalar}(\hat{a}\,N(z))\bigr)$, where $\hat a$ is the idele attached to $a$ and $N$ is the idelic norm of `genuineBaseChange K L`, one has
--   $$\int_{\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)} \varphi\bigl(x^{-1}\,\mathrm{globalPoints}(\delta_0)\,\sigma^{-1}_D(\mathrm{scalar}(z)\,x)\bigr)\,w(x)\,d\,\mathrm{adelicGLHaar}(x) = I.$$
--
--   Fourth, there is a continuous, compactly supported $G : (\mathbb{A}_K)^\times \to \mathbb{C}$ such that for every idele $u$ of $K$ the value $G(u)$ is an orbital integral, for $c_0 \cdot$ `adelicGLHaar`, at $\mathrm{globalPoints}(\gamma_0)$ and with respect to $\tau$, of the function $g \mapsto f(g\,\mathrm{scalar}(u))$.
--
--   This packages, for a single twisted class whose norm class is elliptic, the local transfer data needed in the comparison of the $\sigma$-twisted and ordinary trace formulae for $\mathrm{GL}_2$ in a base change of prime degree: a matched pair of Haar measures on the twisted centraliser and the centraliser, the logarithmic growth of their band covolumes (with the factor $1/[L:K]$ on the twisted side), section functions realising the twisted orbital integral as the corresponding orbital integral at the norm, and continuity and compact support of the orbital integral as a function of the central idele. It is used by [`AutomorphicForm.setIntegral_mul_setIntegral_sigmaCentralizerDomain_eq_mul_sum_setIntegral_range_idelicNorm_of_normClassMap_eq_of_areMatchingOn`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.setIntegral_mul_setIntegral_sigmaCentralizerDomain_eq_mul_sum_setIntegral_range_idelicNorm_of_normClassMap_eq_of_areMatchingOn) in the elliptic term comparison.
